WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.488
- Never stop learning.

00:00:02.488 --> 00:00:06.371
We see HelloFresh everyday as
an new learning opportunity.

00:00:06.371 --> 00:00:08.851
I think the moment that you
stop learning and developing

00:00:08.851 --> 00:00:10.480
is the moment in which the company

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.349
ultimately is going to stop growing and

00:00:12.349 --> 00:00:14.028
improving as you want it to.

00:00:14.028 --> 00:00:16.421
(electronic music)

00:00:16.421 --> 00:00:17.254
I'm Ed Boyes.

00:00:17.254 --> 00:00:20.200
I run the US operations at HelloFresh.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.556
HelloFresh is an online
grocery delivery service.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:26.061
We make it easier for people to cook

00:00:26.061 --> 00:00:28.840
delicious recipes at home.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.811
We do that by eliminating
every single obstacle

00:00:31.811 --> 00:00:33.509
that you have to home cooking.

00:00:33.509 --> 00:00:35.931
Our consumers don't like
going to the grocery store,

00:00:35.931 --> 00:00:37.731
don't like waiting in a line.

00:00:37.731 --> 00:00:40.800
They struggle to find new
recipes and new ideas.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.120
So we take all of those
struggles away from them

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.291
by sending them a box with
the exact fresh ingredients

00:00:46.291 --> 00:00:50.480
and step-by-step recipes to
make it really easy and simple.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.067
So I joined the team at the very beginning

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:55.131
to launch and run the UK business.

00:00:55.131 --> 00:00:59.054
We started very early on
in several European markets

00:00:59.054 --> 00:01:02.066
really kind of try to
figure out the concept

00:01:02.066 --> 00:01:03.149
and how it works.

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:06.098
We had a really successful
few years in Europe,

00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:08.459
and then over the course of
the last couple of years,

00:01:08.459 --> 00:01:10.330
we really expanded in the US,

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:13.984
so I went over to run the US operation.

00:01:13.984 --> 00:01:18.825
Now we deliver over nine million
meals per month globally.

00:01:18.825 --> 00:01:20.514
So the challenges of being young in

00:01:20.514 --> 00:01:23.263
such a rapidly growing
company in many ways

00:01:23.263 --> 00:01:25.012
I see it more as an opportunity.

00:01:25.012 --> 00:01:27.480
At an earlier stage in your
career, I think you have

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:31.122
the ability to be very agile,
move quickly and evolve.

00:01:31.122 --> 00:01:33.834
We've historically actually hired people

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:37.193
for trajectory rather than
experience level at HelloFresh

00:01:37.193 --> 00:01:38.452
and really if we want to have

00:01:38.452 --> 00:01:40.972
a business which evolves and grows and

00:01:40.972 --> 00:01:43.772
really defines a new
category on a global level,

00:01:43.772 --> 00:01:45.994
we think it's far more
important that people have

00:01:45.994 --> 00:01:49.882
an agile, nimble attitude
to growing the business.

00:01:49.882 --> 00:01:52.314
So I think one of my career highlights

00:01:52.314 --> 00:01:56.631
actually came before my
career even started, so

00:01:56.631 --> 00:02:01.208
I was very keen sportsman
as a teenager growing up,

00:02:01.208 --> 00:02:03.736
and then had a couple
of terrible injuries,

00:02:03.736 --> 00:02:06.787
and those terrible
injuries led me to putting

00:02:06.787 --> 00:02:11.732
my competitive intensity into
entrepreneurial endeavors.

00:02:11.732 --> 00:02:15.032
Started a couple of businesses, age 16,

00:02:15.032 --> 00:02:17.018
completely unsuccessful but really

00:02:17.018 --> 00:02:19.955
gave me the entrepreneurial bug.

00:02:19.955 --> 00:02:22.831
In the early stages of developing
a company from scratch,

00:02:22.831 --> 00:02:24.712
it's really all about hustling.

00:02:24.712 --> 00:02:26.407
You know when you go into corporate life,

00:02:26.407 --> 00:02:28.024
people have three month road maps.

00:02:28.024 --> 00:02:31.172
They have 12-month strategies.

00:02:31.172 --> 00:02:33.100
In starting a new business,
and getting something

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:36.619
off the ground, you don't
even have a one day strategy.

00:02:36.619 --> 00:02:39.986
So it's really about
kind of focusing on the

00:02:39.986 --> 00:02:41.607
imminent challenges ahead of you and

00:02:41.607 --> 00:02:43.548
kind of really hustling and really

00:02:43.548 --> 00:02:45.395
kind of making things happen.

00:02:45.395 --> 00:02:48.312
(electronic music)

